WEBVTT

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.346
Ensign Kim.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.250
I require your assistance
in Jefferies Tube 37-Alpha.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.377
Well, can it wait?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.648
I just got off duty.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.655
It is urgent.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.849
Hmm.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.686
Bridge to Commander Tuvok.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.826
Tuvok here.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.166
You're needed
on the Bridge, sir.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.864
On my way.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.206
Computer, lights on.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.550
Neelix?

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.388
Is anybody here?

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.451
Voyager to Lieutenant Paris.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.620
Paris here.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.493
How's it going out there, Tom?

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:07.466
One more orbit and I should have
all the data we need.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.365
Good work.
See you when you get back.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.801
Chakotay out.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:14.972
Crewman. Ensign.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:16.303
Sir.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.673
Hello, sir.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.130
It looks to me

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.832
like you aligned
the power couplings perfectly.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.033
I did.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.001
If you're so sure,

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.342
then why'd you need
me to look at them?

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.006
I did not.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.278
Then what's this all about?

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:01.219
I've learned from observing
Lieutenants Torres and Paris

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.415
that humans sometimes
require a pretext

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.447
for being intimate
with one another.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.617
Intimate?

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.654
Resistance is futile.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.796
Paris to Voyager.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.967
Voyager here.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.341
My primary warp manifold
just ruptured.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.777
I've lost helm control.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.280
Auxiliary power is off-line.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.804
Thrusters won't respond.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:30.975
Say again, Tom.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.644
Your signal's breaking up.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.913
My orbit's decaying.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.716
I don't think I can hold it.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.813
Repeat that, Tom.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.983
I need an emergency beam-out!

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.960
Voyager to Lieutenant Paris.
Come in!

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.191
Neelix?

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.994
What can I do for you, Captain?

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.595
Where is everybody?

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.005
Didn't you see them
when you came in?

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.008
No.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.373
Take a look.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.985
Computer, activate lights.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.322
Lieutenant Commander Tuvok
reporting for duty.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.701
Is something wrong?

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.967
I think you forgot something,
Tuvok.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:41.176
It appears that, in my haste
to report to the Bridge,

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.815
I neglected
to put on my uniform.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.626
What happened to them?

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.637
They died.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:03:59.831
Why?

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.466
You didn't get them
home in time.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.133
Hello.

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:52.575
Good morning.

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:55.577
Sleep well?

00:06:57.015 --> 00:06:58.482
Not really.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:00.815
What are you doing here?

00:07:00.852 --> 00:07:03.912
I just thought
I'd stop by and ask you

00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:06.456
why you didn't meet me
for breakfast.

00:07:06.491 --> 00:07:07.515
Breakfast...

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:08.924
What time is it?

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:10.153
7:40.

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:13.323
And we were supposed
to meet at 0700.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:14.491
I was there...

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:17.127
right after I got
off the night shift.

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:18.796
I waited... and I waited

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:20.805
and I called you on the com.

00:07:20.839 --> 00:07:22.739
I... uh... I-I
didn't hear you.

00:07:22.774 --> 00:07:24.935
I was having
this wild nightmare.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.477
I was out like a light.

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:29.071
I'm sorry.
I'll get dressed right now.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:30.103
You don't have time.

00:07:30.148 --> 00:07:32.378
You're due
on the Bridge at 0800,

00:07:32.417 --> 00:07:33.645
and I've got to get some sleep.

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:34.652
Oh, I hate this!

00:07:34.686 --> 00:07:37.314
We never see each other.

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:41.660
I'm off Friday night.

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:43.192
Great.

00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:44.855
Let's go skiing.

00:07:44.896 --> 00:07:47.456
How about Saint Moritz?

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:49.160
We went skiing last time.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.462
And you loved it.

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:52.436
You're getting
really good, you know.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.961
I just thought maybe
we could run a program

00:07:55.073 --> 00:07:58.133
where the wind chill factor
wasn't 30 below zero...

00:07:58.176 --> 00:08:00.371
like... Fiji

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:01.470
or Samoa.

00:08:01.513 --> 00:08:03.310
Oh. There's nothing to do there.

00:08:03.348 --> 00:08:07.478
And you can be warm
while you're not doing it.

00:08:07.519 --> 00:08:10.147
How about a compromise?

00:08:10.188 --> 00:08:11.450
Um...

00:08:11.489 --> 00:08:13.150
spring skiing in Chile?

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:14.283
Much warmer.

00:08:14.325 --> 00:08:17.260
A compromise...

00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:20.628
How about Tahiti?

00:08:20.665 --> 00:08:22.530
Hmm. Tahiti.

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:26.902
As long as I can
go waterskiing, fine.

00:08:26.938 --> 00:08:28.200
You're on.

00:08:33.211 --> 00:08:34.508
Now, go get dressed,

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:37.674
so you'll at least have time
to stop for some coffee.

00:08:37.716 --> 00:08:39.843
I'll see you Friday night.

00:08:48.059 --> 00:08:48.957
Morning, Tom.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:49.958
Mm.

00:08:50.061 --> 00:08:51.085
What will it be?

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:52.619
Scrambled, sunny-side up,
over easy?

00:08:52.664 --> 00:08:54.291
Just a cup of coffee.

00:08:54.332 --> 00:08:55.299
Are you sure?

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:56.527
Breakfast is
the most important meal

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:57.535
of the day, you know.

00:08:57.569 --> 00:08:58.661
Neelix!

00:08:58.703 --> 00:08:59.829
Right.

00:09:10.281 --> 00:09:11.248
Uh...

00:09:11.282 --> 00:09:12.374
Neelix...

00:09:12.417 --> 00:09:14.783
did you have a rough night
or something?

00:09:14.819 --> 00:09:16.184
Why do you ask?

00:09:16.221 --> 00:09:19.452
Because you just poured me
a steaming cup of cooking oil.

00:09:23.194 --> 00:09:24.320
Actually, I did have

00:09:24.362 --> 00:09:26.557
a little trouble sleeping
last night.

00:09:26.598 --> 00:09:27.690
Nightmares.

00:09:27.732 --> 00:09:28.699
Oh.

00:09:28.733 --> 00:09:30.633
Me, too.

00:09:30.668 --> 00:09:32.727
Must have been
those three full moons

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:33.931
we passed yesterday.

00:09:33.972 --> 00:09:35.633
Well, a few sips of my coffee

00:09:35.673 --> 00:09:37.937
should clear the fuzz
out of your brain.

00:09:38.009 --> 00:09:40.569
Maybe you should pour yourself
a cup while you're at it.

00:09:52.957 --> 00:09:55.118
Seem to be
a little shorthanded today.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.957
Tom and Harry are both late.

00:09:57.028 --> 00:09:58.689
I was going to give them
another five minutes,

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.254
but I'll call them now,
if you'd like.

00:10:00.298 --> 00:10:00.957
That's all right.

00:10:01.032 --> 00:10:02.499
I'm a little late myself,
aren't I?

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:04.525
I wasn't going to mention it.

00:10:04.569 --> 00:10:06.332
Burning the midnight oil?

00:10:06.371 --> 00:10:07.963
Actually, I went to bed early
for a change,

00:10:08.006 --> 00:10:10.668
but I had a nightmare and
I could not get back to sleep.

00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:12.676
I had a bad dream
last night, too.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.440
You tell me yours and
I'll tell you mine.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.311
Sorry I'm late, Captain.

00:10:19.584 --> 00:10:21.643
Well?

00:10:21.686 --> 00:10:23.847
I was in the forest
with my father.

00:10:23.888 --> 00:10:27.915
We were hunting deer,
which was odd,

00:10:27.959 --> 00:10:30.519
because that was something
I always refused to do.

00:10:30.562 --> 00:10:31.824
We cornered the animal.

00:10:31.863 --> 00:10:34.889
I looked to my father to see
if he was going to kill it,

00:10:34.933 --> 00:10:36.730
but he wasn't my father anymore.

00:10:36.768 --> 00:10:38.497
He was a vicious-looking alien.

00:10:38.536 --> 00:10:41.096
There was an alien
in my dream, too.

00:10:41.139 --> 00:10:44.370
And it wasn't from any race
I've seen before.

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:45.808
He had...

00:10:45.844 --> 00:10:49.712
sharp ridges on his forehead
and on the front of his neck.

00:10:49.747 --> 00:10:51.681
That's what mine looked like.

00:10:51.716 --> 00:10:54.150
I don't mean
to be eavesdropping, but...

00:10:54.185 --> 00:10:56.153
I had a nightmare last night,
too,

00:10:56.187 --> 00:10:58.621
and I'm pretty sure
I saw the same guy.

00:11:00.158 --> 00:11:01.182
Tuvok?

00:11:01.226 --> 00:11:02.523
By any chance

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.858
did you have a bad dream
last night?

00:11:04.896 --> 00:11:08.696
I did have a somewhat
unsettling dream, yes.

00:11:08.733 --> 00:11:11.463
It involved an alien
with ridges

00:11:11.502 --> 00:11:13.333
on his face and neck.

00:11:13.371 --> 00:11:17.137
I'd say this sounds like
more than a coincidence.

00:11:17.175 --> 00:11:18.972
Let's get the rest
of the senior staff together

00:11:19.077 --> 00:11:20.305
and come up with some answers.

00:11:20.345 --> 00:11:21.505
Which reminds me, where's Harry?

00:11:21.546 --> 00:11:23.741
Bridge to Ensign Kim.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:27.443
Computer, locate Ensign Kim.

00:11:27.485 --> 00:11:29.612
Ensign Kim is in his quarters.

00:11:29.654 --> 00:11:31.087
Tuvok.

00:11:35.927 --> 00:11:38.395
Deck 6.

00:11:38.429 --> 00:11:39.896
I've got a hunch

00:11:39.931 --> 00:11:42.900
Harry's dreaming about
our new alien friend.

00:11:42.934 --> 00:11:45.459
That would be consistent
with the experiences

00:11:45.503 --> 00:11:46.993
the rest of us have had.

00:11:47.071 --> 00:11:48.766
Tell me more about your dream.

00:11:48.806 --> 00:11:50.865
Where exactly did
you see the alien?

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:52.570
As a matter of fact, it
was here in the turbolift.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:53.872
What happened?

00:11:53.912 --> 00:11:55.937
The alien simply stared at me

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.278
as if scrutinizing
my appearance.

00:11:58.316 --> 00:12:00.011
That's what happened
in my dream.

00:12:00.051 --> 00:12:01.075
What did you do?

00:12:01.119 --> 00:12:03.849
I returned to my quarters.

00:12:03.888 --> 00:12:05.719
Did the alien follow you?

00:12:05.757 --> 00:12:08.123
He did.

00:12:08.159 --> 00:12:09.421
And then?

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.758
He watched me.

00:12:11.796 --> 00:12:13.127
Doing what?

00:12:14.632 --> 00:12:16.099
Getting dressed.

00:12:17.902 --> 00:12:19.870
Getting dressed?

00:12:19.904 --> 00:12:22.099
Yes.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:26.600
I don't suppose I should ask
why you were undressed.

00:12:26.644 --> 00:12:28.976
I would prefer that you didn't.

00:12:41.092 --> 00:12:42.559
Harry?

00:12:44.595 --> 00:12:45.755
Harry?

00:12:45.797 --> 00:12:47.992
Computer, open door 105-2.

00:12:48.032 --> 00:12:51.229
Security clearance:
Tuvok-zeta-nine.

00:12:59.877 --> 00:13:01.640
Harry?

00:13:06.617 --> 00:13:09.245
Harry, wake up.

00:13:18.129 --> 00:13:19.596
Are they comatose?

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:20.927
Not exactly.

00:13:20.965 --> 00:13:24.162
They all appear to be
in a hyper-REM state.

00:13:24.202 --> 00:13:26.363
I've tried every conventional
method of waking them...

00:13:26.404 --> 00:13:28.372
from drugs to direct
cortical stimulation...

00:13:28.406 --> 00:13:29.532
but nothing works.

00:13:29.574 --> 00:13:31.804
Do you have any idea
what's causing this?

00:13:31.843 --> 00:13:35.870
Scans haven't detected
any viral or bacterial agents.

00:13:35.913 --> 00:13:38.939
No cranial trauma,
no neural disorders.

00:13:38.983 --> 00:13:41.042
They're simply... asleep.

00:13:48.893 --> 00:13:50.554
I'd say it's a pretty good bet

00:13:50.595 --> 00:13:53.996
this is somehow related
to the alien from our dreams.

00:13:54.065 --> 00:13:55.999
Any progress
in identifying him?

00:13:56.067 --> 00:13:57.864
Not yet, but I've got
everyone working on it.

00:13:57.902 --> 00:14:00.234
In the meantime, what's
your recommendation?

00:14:00.271 --> 00:14:02.205
Large doses of animazine.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.140
I thought you said
drugs weren't working.

00:14:04.175 --> 00:14:06.075
Not for them.
For everybody else.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.271
Until I can determine
what's happening

00:14:08.312 --> 00:14:11.179
I'd suggest the rest of you
avoid going to sleep.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:19.849
I'd say his ridges were
a little more pronounced.

00:14:19.891 --> 00:14:22.689
Computer, increase
facial ridge height

00:14:22.727 --> 00:14:24.854
by four centimeters.

00:14:24.896 --> 00:14:27.160
That's closer.

00:14:27.198 --> 00:14:29.291
I think his eyes
were wider apart.

00:14:29.333 --> 00:14:32.097
Computer, increase the space
between the eyes

00:14:32.136 --> 00:14:34.502
by three centimeters.

00:14:34.539 --> 00:14:38.031
Increase skin color and texture.

00:14:39.944 --> 00:14:41.241
That's him.

00:14:41.279 --> 00:14:44.077
Has anybody seen
this species before?

00:14:44.115 --> 00:14:46.208
While you were awake, I mean.

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.274
Seven?

00:14:47.318 --> 00:14:50.879
He doesn't resemble any species
assimilated by the Borg.

00:14:50.922 --> 00:14:53.482
So is he just
a figment of our imagination?

00:14:53.524 --> 00:14:56.891
If he is, we've all been
imagining the exact same thing.

00:14:56.928 --> 00:14:58.259
One possible explanation

00:14:58.296 --> 00:15:01.060
is that he's attempting
to make telepathic contact.

00:15:01.099 --> 00:15:03.067
He's doing more
than making contact.

00:15:03.101 --> 00:15:05.569
We've got six crew members
who can't wake up.

00:15:05.603 --> 00:15:07.935
For all we know,
it's some sort of attack.

00:15:08.039 --> 00:15:09.301
From where?

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.774
Astrometric scans
haven't revealed any ships

00:15:11.809 --> 00:15:13.037
in this vicinity

00:15:13.077 --> 00:15:15.272
or planets capable
of sustaining humanoid life.

00:15:15.313 --> 00:15:18.111
So where do we look?

00:15:18.149 --> 00:15:19.275
In our dreams.

00:15:19.317 --> 00:15:23.617
That's the only place
any of us have seen him, right?

00:15:23.654 --> 00:15:25.121
So, if we want
to communicate with him...

00:15:25.156 --> 00:15:26.123
find out what he wants...

00:15:26.157 --> 00:15:27.317
we'll have to do it
on his terms.

00:15:27.358 --> 00:15:29.826
How do you propose we do that?

00:15:31.329 --> 00:15:32.557
Lucid dreaming.

00:15:32.597 --> 00:15:33.962
What's that?

00:15:34.031 --> 00:15:35.794
It's a technique

00:15:35.833 --> 00:15:37.968
which allows you
to take control of your dream.

00:15:38.101 --> 00:15:39.363
That happened to me once.

00:15:39.402 --> 00:15:41.302
I dreamt I was falling

00:15:41.338 --> 00:15:43.499
and suddenly I realized
that I was dreaming

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.839
and I could fly, land...
do whatever I wanted.

00:15:46.876 --> 00:15:48.844
I was in complete
control of the dream.

00:15:48.878 --> 00:15:50.243
What happened to you by accident

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.804
is something some people
can do by design.

00:15:51.848 --> 00:15:53.941
I've been able
to have a lucid dream

00:15:53.984 --> 00:15:56.646
by using the same technology
I use for a vision quest.

00:15:56.686 --> 00:16:00.087
I may be able to use it
to communicate with this alien.

00:16:00.123 --> 00:16:01.647
Maybe so.

00:16:01.691 --> 00:16:04.319
But how do we know you'd
be able to wake up again?

00:16:04.361 --> 00:16:06.591
It's kind of like self-hypnosis.

00:16:06.629 --> 00:16:09.120
Before I go to sleep,
I choose a visual cue...

00:16:09.165 --> 00:16:11.360
something to let me
know I'm dreaming...

00:16:11.401 --> 00:16:12.390
Earth's moon, say.

00:16:12.435 --> 00:16:13.925
Once I see it, I can wake myself

00:16:14.037 --> 00:16:16.198
by tapping the back
of my hand three times.

00:16:16.239 --> 00:16:17.831
Perhaps you are capable

00:16:17.874 --> 00:16:20.104
of doing this under
normal circumstances,

00:16:20.143 --> 00:16:22.304
but these were hardly
conventional dreams

00:16:22.345 --> 00:16:23.312
we experienced.

00:16:23.346 --> 00:16:24.574
I don't see any other way

00:16:24.614 --> 00:16:26.912
of finding out
what our friend here is after,

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:29.282
or how we can wake up
Harry and the others.

00:16:29.319 --> 00:16:31.617
Besides, we can't stay awake
forever.

00:16:33.189 --> 00:16:36.625
You'll do this in Sick Bay
under the Doctor's supervision.

00:16:36.659 --> 00:16:38.058
The rest of you keep
scanning the region.

00:16:38.094 --> 00:16:40.528
Analyze this ship
from stem to stern.

00:16:40.563 --> 00:16:43.191
Wherever he is, find him.

00:16:43.233 --> 00:16:44.222
Come on.

00:16:47.337 --> 00:16:49.168
Normally, I consider
a good night's sleep

00:16:49.205 --> 00:16:51.332
an important part
of any health regimen,

00:16:51.374 --> 00:16:53.968
but in this case,
I can't recommend it.

00:16:54.044 --> 00:16:56.171
I respect your
medical opinion, Doctor.

00:16:56.212 --> 00:16:58.077
But at this point,
we're out of options.

00:16:59.282 --> 00:17:01.546
This will regulate
your hypothalamus.

00:17:01.584 --> 00:17:04.610
But in all probability,
I won't be able to wake you.

00:17:04.654 --> 00:17:05.780
You'll be on your own.

00:17:05.822 --> 00:17:07.221
I understand.

00:17:09.893 --> 00:17:11.224
Ready?

00:17:14.197 --> 00:17:15.755
Pleasant dreams.

00:17:19.436 --> 00:17:21.495
Ah-koo-chee-moya.

00:17:21.538 --> 00:17:25.440
Far from the sacred places
of my grandfathers,

00:17:25.475 --> 00:17:28.308
far from the bones of my people,

00:17:28.344 --> 00:17:30.869
I seek to sleep,

00:17:30.914 --> 00:17:34.281
to meet the one who has
visited us in our dreams.

00:19:03.806 --> 00:19:06.741
I know this is a dream...
my dream.

00:19:06.776 --> 00:19:07.800
I'm in control.

00:19:07.844 --> 00:19:08.811
You're mistaken.

00:19:08.845 --> 00:19:10.210
Am I?

00:19:10.246 --> 00:19:11.713
This is more than a dream.

00:19:11.748 --> 00:19:13.113
It's my reality

00:19:13.149 --> 00:19:14.844
and you're no different
than the others.

00:19:14.884 --> 00:19:15.873
"The others?"

00:19:15.919 --> 00:19:17.614
The waking species.

00:19:17.654 --> 00:19:19.519
For centuries, you've
come and found us

00:19:19.556 --> 00:19:21.114
in a state that you call "sleep"

00:19:21.157 --> 00:19:24.149
and tried to destroy
us, but not anymore.

00:19:24.194 --> 00:19:26.458
Now we are in control.

00:19:26.496 --> 00:19:30.159
One by one, you will fall asleep
and enter our reality,

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.293
where it is you
who will be destroyed.

00:19:34.304 --> 00:19:35.931
We didn't attack you.

00:19:36.005 --> 00:19:37.267
We didn't even know you existed

00:19:37.307 --> 00:19:39.070
until we started seeing
you in our dreams.

00:19:39.108 --> 00:19:43.135
Tell me how I can wake my crew
and I promise we'll leave.

00:19:43.179 --> 00:19:45.477
As long as you're asleep,
you're no threat to us.

00:19:45.515 --> 00:19:48.109
I can wake myself
anytime I want,

00:19:48.151 --> 00:19:50.949
and if I do...

00:19:50.987 --> 00:19:52.318
I'm going to start
looking for you

00:19:52.355 --> 00:19:53.879
in the waking world...

00:19:53.923 --> 00:19:55.481
find where you're sleeping.

00:19:55.525 --> 00:19:57.254
You wouldn't want that.

00:19:58.761 --> 00:20:00.956
Leave our space.

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:03.692
Once you're beyond it,
your people will awaken.

00:20:03.733 --> 00:20:05.098
Just tell me
how far we need to go.

00:20:05.134 --> 00:20:07.602
There's a six-planet system
less than a parsec away.

00:20:07.637 --> 00:20:10.231
It marks the nearest border
of our space.

00:20:10.273 --> 00:20:12.332
We can be past it in one day.

00:20:12.375 --> 00:20:13.967
Then wake yourself...

00:20:14.077 --> 00:20:17.843
and pray you never
dream of us again.

00:20:22.485 --> 00:20:23.645
Congratulations, Commander.

00:20:23.686 --> 00:20:24.653
You're awake.

00:20:25.688 --> 00:20:26.848
Chakotay.

00:20:26.889 --> 00:20:28.754
I'm fine.

00:20:28.791 --> 00:20:30.986
The alien... did you see him?

00:20:31.027 --> 00:20:33.120
And?

00:20:33.162 --> 00:20:34.129
Well, it was certainly

00:20:34.163 --> 00:20:35.926
one of the most interesting
away missions

00:20:35.965 --> 00:20:36.932
I've ever been on.

00:20:36.966 --> 00:20:39.264
I'll tell you about it
on the way to the Bridge.

00:20:49.012 --> 00:20:51.207
Tuvok, scan
for a six-planet system.

00:20:51.247 --> 00:20:53.010
It should be less
than a parsec from here.

00:20:53.082 --> 00:20:56.745
I have it, Captain,
at coordinates 139 mark 42.

00:20:56.786 --> 00:20:59.254
Tom, lay in a course.

00:20:59.289 --> 00:21:00.586
Aye, Captain.

00:21:01.691 --> 00:21:02.817
Course laid in.

00:21:02.859 --> 00:21:04.417
Do you mind if I ask
where we're heading?

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.155
Past the aliens' territory.

00:21:06.195 --> 00:21:08.561
Once we're clear of it, Harry
and the others should wake up.

00:21:08.598 --> 00:21:10.930
And the rest of us
can finally get some sleep.

00:21:10.967 --> 00:21:13.060
One step at a time, Tom.

00:21:15.104 --> 00:21:16.765
From what the alien told me,

00:21:16.806 --> 00:21:18.603
it sounds like they
have corporeal form,

00:21:18.641 --> 00:21:20.472
but they communicate
through their dreams.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:22.603
For them, it's as real
as the waking world.

00:21:22.645 --> 00:21:24.442
Extraordinary.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.175
It reminds me
of the Australian Aborigines.

00:21:26.215 --> 00:21:27.409
They believed the dream world

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.475
was no more or less real
than the waking world.

00:21:29.519 --> 00:21:31.578
In fact,
their creation mythology says

00:21:31.621 --> 00:21:34.784
their ancestors actually dreamed
the universe into existence.

00:21:34.824 --> 00:21:35.984
That's mythology.

00:21:36.092 --> 00:21:37.855
This seems to be fact.

00:21:39.629 --> 00:21:40.994
I wonder...

00:21:41.064 --> 00:21:42.224
do they ever wake up?

00:21:42.265 --> 00:21:43.994
How did they evolve this way?

00:21:44.033 --> 00:21:45.557
We may never know.

00:21:45.601 --> 00:21:48.764
Sometimes first contact
is last contact.

00:21:59.148 --> 00:22:01.639
We're approaching the border
of the aliens' space.

00:22:01.684 --> 00:22:03.845
Commander Tuvok,
inform the Doctor.

00:22:03.886 --> 00:22:05.854
Aye, Captain.

00:22:09.192 --> 00:22:11.251
Wake up, Ensign.

00:22:14.697 --> 00:22:16.164
What's going on?

00:22:16.199 --> 00:22:17.325
You were napping.

00:22:19.168 --> 00:22:20.635
In Sick Bay?

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:22.763
We had to move you here
when we couldn't wake you.

00:22:25.141 --> 00:22:26.608
Whew.

00:22:26.642 --> 00:22:27.768
How long?

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:28.868
17 hours.

00:22:28.911 --> 00:22:30.811
I take it you
experienced nightmares

00:22:30.847 --> 00:22:32.212
like the rest of the crew.

00:22:32.248 --> 00:22:34.307
Oh, I had nightmares, all right.

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:36.181
Tell me about them.

00:22:36.219 --> 00:22:37.811
Well...

00:22:37.854 --> 00:22:41.722
I was, uh, in the corridor...

00:22:44.627 --> 00:22:46.822
Captain Janeway asked me
to bring you the results

00:22:46.863 --> 00:22:47.989
of our astrometric scans.

00:22:48.064 --> 00:22:49.326
She thought
they might be helpful

00:22:49.365 --> 00:22:51.697
in determining the precise cause
of the crew's somnolence.

00:22:51.734 --> 00:22:52.996
Thank you.

00:22:53.035 --> 00:22:54.229
Ensign Kim,
now that you're awake,

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:56.898
I require your assistance
in Jefferies Tube 21-Beta.

00:22:58.808 --> 00:23:01.003
Is something wrong?

00:23:01.043 --> 00:23:04.376
No. I, um...

00:23:04.414 --> 00:23:06.882
I'm still feeling
a little groggy.

00:23:06.916 --> 00:23:09.043
Then, I'll wait
until you are fully recovered.

00:23:10.486 --> 00:23:11.612
Now, then, Ensign,

00:23:11.654 --> 00:23:13.884
you were telling me
about your nightmare.

00:23:16.826 --> 00:23:18.123
You know what, Doc? Um...

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:25.157
I'm... famished.

00:23:26.202 --> 00:23:28.500
Haven't eaten
in at least 17 hours, right?

00:23:28.538 --> 00:23:30.165
Very well.

00:23:30.206 --> 00:23:33.232
Go eat, get some clothes on
and report back in an hour.

00:23:33.276 --> 00:23:35.176
I'll see you later.

00:23:35.211 --> 00:23:36.405
You too, Seven.

00:23:39.515 --> 00:23:42.245
And the next thing I knew,
I was being boiled alive

00:23:42.285 --> 00:23:44.753
in a pot
of my own leola root stew.

00:23:44.787 --> 00:23:46.550
Talk about a nightmare.

00:23:46.589 --> 00:23:48.614
Well, it was perfectly seasoned.

00:23:52.093 --> 00:23:55.722
Well, if it isn't
Sleeping Beauty.

00:23:55.763 --> 00:23:57.321
I do look well-rested, don't I?

00:23:57.365 --> 00:23:58.798
Is everyone awake now?

00:23:58.833 --> 00:24:01.393
The Doc checked us all out
and says we're fine.

00:24:01.436 --> 00:24:02.494
Have a seat.

00:24:02.537 --> 00:24:05.097
We were just trading
dream stories.

00:24:05.139 --> 00:24:06.299
Tell us yours.

00:24:06.341 --> 00:24:08.138
Oh. It was...

00:24:08.176 --> 00:24:10.167
nothing very interesting.

00:24:10.211 --> 00:24:11.576
Just the usual...

00:24:11.612 --> 00:24:12.943
You know, uh...

00:24:13.047 --> 00:24:14.412
Who was she, Harry?

00:24:17.852 --> 00:24:19.342
The woman of my dreams.

00:24:21.923 --> 00:24:26.485
What I'd like to know
is what Tuvok dreamt about.

00:24:26.527 --> 00:24:28.256
Yes, Commander, tell us.

00:24:28.296 --> 00:24:30.230
What do Vulcans dream?

00:24:30.264 --> 00:24:32.459
Aren't you supposed
to have horrible nightmares?

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:35.901
I wonder what a Vulcan nightmare
would be like?

00:24:35.937 --> 00:24:38.838
Alone, exiled on a planet

00:24:38.873 --> 00:24:41.899
where the only form
of communication...

00:24:41.943 --> 00:24:43.376
is laughter.

00:24:46.347 --> 00:24:47.439
Oh, come on, Tuvok.

00:24:47.482 --> 00:24:51.418
I won't dignify this inquisition
with a response.

00:24:53.755 --> 00:24:54.744
Red Alert.

00:24:54.789 --> 00:24:56.984
All hands to battle stations.

00:24:57.025 --> 00:24:58.890
They're coming around
for another pass.

00:24:58.926 --> 00:25:00.894
Auxiliary power to the shields.

00:25:03.998 --> 00:25:05.693
Return fire.

00:25:08.569 --> 00:25:10.799
No damage to the alien ship.

00:25:10.838 --> 00:25:12.237
Our phasers can't penetrate
their shields.

00:25:12.273 --> 00:25:13.934
Arm photon torpedoes.

00:25:13.975 --> 00:25:15.101
We seem to have a knack

00:25:15.143 --> 00:25:16.872
for provoking strangers
these days.

00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:19.938
Shields are off-line.

00:25:20.048 --> 00:25:20.980
Fire.

00:25:23.785 --> 00:25:25.480
I've lost power
to the torpedo launchers.

00:25:25.520 --> 00:25:26.919
What's happening?

00:25:26.954 --> 00:25:29.752
Power is being drained
from all systems.

00:25:29.791 --> 00:25:31.156
We're being hailed.

00:25:31.192 --> 00:25:33.092
On screen.

00:25:33.127 --> 00:25:34.321
Captain.

00:25:34.362 --> 00:25:35.386
Ensign Kim.

00:25:35.430 --> 00:25:36.897
Commander Chakotay.

00:25:36.931 --> 00:25:41.027
I'm glad to see you
all up and about.

00:25:46.641 --> 00:25:47.972
Janeway to Engineering.

00:25:48.042 --> 00:25:50.602
We need auxiliary power
to the engines now.

00:25:50.645 --> 00:25:52.613
I think you'll find
that impossible.

00:25:52.647 --> 00:25:53.841
B'Elanna, report.

00:25:53.881 --> 00:25:54.905
There's a localized

00:25:54.949 --> 00:25:56.507
dampening field
around the ship, Captain.

00:25:56.551 --> 00:25:59.281
I can't give you engines,
weapons, shields...

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:00.787
Everything you told me
was a lie.

00:26:00.822 --> 00:26:03.586
This was all an elaborate trap
to get Voyager here.

00:26:03.624 --> 00:26:07.492
It appears you're learning
more about my people after all.

00:26:07.528 --> 00:26:10.053
Prepare to surrender your ship.

00:26:10.098 --> 00:26:13.397
Captain, three more
alien vessels are approaching.

00:26:13.434 --> 00:26:15.368
They are powering weapons.

00:26:15.403 --> 00:26:18.634
You've gone to so much trouble
to commandeer this ship.

00:26:18.673 --> 00:26:21.198
I don't think
you're going to destroy it.

00:26:21.242 --> 00:26:23.107
I won't need to.

00:26:28.850 --> 00:26:30.875
Janeway to the crew.
We're under attack.

00:26:30.918 --> 00:26:33.182
Implement defense procedure
omega.

00:26:33.221 --> 00:26:34.381
It's no use.

00:26:34.422 --> 00:26:35.946
We've taken every deck.

00:26:35.990 --> 00:26:38.322
The ship is ours.

00:26:53.808 --> 00:26:55.241
Captain.

00:27:02.650 --> 00:27:04.447
All the time I thought
I was negotiating,

00:27:04.485 --> 00:27:06.453
they were just setting us up
to fly right into their web.

00:27:06.487 --> 00:27:07.920
You couldn't have known
it was a trick.

00:27:08.022 --> 00:27:09.114
I don't understand.

00:27:09.157 --> 00:27:11.091
They exist in dreams
and reality?

00:27:11.125 --> 00:27:12.456
Apparently, entering our dreams

00:27:12.493 --> 00:27:13.926
was their way
to learn about us...

00:27:13.961 --> 00:27:15.929
perhaps to probe our weaknesses.

00:27:15.963 --> 00:27:17.828
Not to mention lure
us into an ambush.

00:27:17.865 --> 00:27:19.492
We need to retake the ship.

00:27:19.534 --> 00:27:21.263
That means getting
out of this cargo bay.

00:27:21.302 --> 00:27:23.167
I checked the Jefferies tubes.
They're sealed.

00:27:23.204 --> 00:27:24.865
Maybe we can open them manually.

00:27:24.906 --> 00:27:26.271
That's not going to be easy.

00:27:26.307 --> 00:27:27.433
They've got people everywhere.

00:27:27.475 --> 00:27:29.602
We'll have to create
a diversion.

00:27:29.644 --> 00:27:30.941
Any ideas?

00:27:30.978 --> 00:27:32.843
I have one, Captain.

00:27:36.751 --> 00:27:38.810
What the hell are you doing?!

00:27:38.853 --> 00:27:40.753
Creating a diversion.

00:27:40.788 --> 00:27:45.487
Ensign Kim, it is your fault
we have been captured.

00:27:47.228 --> 00:27:49.196
I suggest you fight back.

00:27:53.100 --> 00:27:55.091
Tom...

00:27:55.136 --> 00:27:56.831
try to get
into a Jefferies tube.

00:27:56.871 --> 00:27:58.566
You two work on the power grid.

00:27:58.606 --> 00:27:59.800
I'll deal with this.

00:28:01.576 --> 00:28:02.543
Stop, stop!

00:28:02.577 --> 00:28:03.669
What's going on here?

00:28:03.711 --> 00:28:05.042
These are my people.
I'll handle them.

00:28:05.079 --> 00:28:06.410
Ensign, that's enough.
Move!

00:28:25.399 --> 00:28:26.696
What's wrong?

00:28:26.734 --> 00:28:27.860
I'm still asleep.

00:28:27.902 --> 00:28:29.893
What are you talking about?

00:28:32.607 --> 00:28:33.505
Chakotay!

00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:45.314
Commander Chakotay,
you're awake.

00:28:45.353 --> 00:28:46.786
Am I?

00:28:46.821 --> 00:28:48.220
Are you sure?

00:28:48.256 --> 00:28:49.348
Of course you are.

00:28:55.630 --> 00:28:57.120
What are you looking for?

00:28:57.164 --> 00:28:58.131
The moon.

00:28:58.165 --> 00:28:59.154
What?

00:29:03.771 --> 00:29:05.170
I don't see it.

00:29:07.742 --> 00:29:08.902
Where's the Captain?

00:29:09.010 --> 00:29:10.170
Asleep...

00:29:10.211 --> 00:29:11.735
along with the rest of the crew.

00:29:11.779 --> 00:29:12.768
All of them?

00:29:12.813 --> 00:29:13.780
Except me.

00:29:13.814 --> 00:29:15.213
No rest for the never-weary.

00:29:15.249 --> 00:29:16.477
What happened?

00:29:16.517 --> 00:29:18.917
As soon as you entered
your lucid dream,

00:29:18.953 --> 00:29:20.921
they all began falling
asleep one by one.

00:29:20.955 --> 00:29:23.321
I've been trying every method
I can think of to revive them,

00:29:23.357 --> 00:29:24.449
but nothing works.

00:29:24.492 --> 00:29:26.255
It's been 39 hours.

00:29:26.294 --> 00:29:28.057
I've been asleep
for almost two days?

00:29:28.095 --> 00:29:29.756
If I can't wake them soon,

00:29:29.797 --> 00:29:32.357
I'm going to have to start
feeding them intravenously.

00:29:32.400 --> 00:29:35.096
They let me think I was awake,
but I was still dreaming.

00:29:35.136 --> 00:29:36.296
You weren't the only one.

00:29:36.337 --> 00:29:38.202
Look at this.

00:29:38.239 --> 00:29:39.934
What is it?

00:29:39.974 --> 00:29:41.942
A neurogenic field
created by heightened

00:29:42.043 --> 00:29:43.476
electrical activity
in the brain.

00:29:43.511 --> 00:29:45.206
It's been occurring in all

00:29:45.246 --> 00:29:47.806
the sleeping crew members...
and that's not all.

00:29:47.848 --> 00:29:51.113
This is Ensign Kim's
brain wave pattern, indicating

00:29:51.152 --> 00:29:53.416
that he's dreaming
in a hyper-REM state.

00:29:53.454 --> 00:29:56.514
This is Crewman Foster's
pattern.

00:29:56.557 --> 00:29:58.320
They're identical.

00:29:58.359 --> 00:30:03.353
Lieutenant Torres, Captain
Janeway, Commander Tuvok...

00:30:03.397 --> 00:30:05.957
I don't know what it means.

00:30:06.033 --> 00:30:08.661
I think I do.

00:30:08.703 --> 00:30:11.866
Not only are they dreaming,

00:30:11.906 --> 00:30:14.466
they're all having
the same dream.

00:30:20.381 --> 00:30:21.348
It wasn't just my dream.

00:30:21.382 --> 00:30:22.349
It was a communal dream.

00:30:22.383 --> 00:30:23.782
Everyone's REM patterns
are identical.

00:30:23.818 --> 00:30:25.513
They're experiencing
the same images,

00:30:25.553 --> 00:30:27.487
each from his or her
own point of view.

00:30:27.521 --> 00:30:29.352
Yes. I saw the rest
of the crew...

00:30:29.390 --> 00:30:30.516
interacted with them.

00:30:30.558 --> 00:30:33.721
We were all working together
to fight off an alien attack.

00:30:33.761 --> 00:30:34.785
Which wasn't real.

00:30:34.829 --> 00:30:36.091
Oh, we're under attack,
all right.

00:30:36.130 --> 00:30:37.324
Commander?

00:30:37.365 --> 00:30:38.423
Maybe this is the way

00:30:38.466 --> 00:30:40.127
these aliens
fight their enemies.

00:30:40.167 --> 00:30:42.431
They exist somewhere
in our reality

00:30:42.470 --> 00:30:43.528
as physical beings,

00:30:43.571 --> 00:30:47.007
but they must be asleep,
unable to defend themselves

00:30:47.041 --> 00:30:48.872
against what they call
"waking species."

00:30:48.909 --> 00:30:51.776
We'll never defeat them
in their dream reality,

00:30:51.812 --> 00:30:54.280
but if we can find them,
find where they're sleeping,

00:30:54.315 --> 00:30:55.407
we'll have the advantage.

00:30:55.449 --> 00:30:56.507
But we've been scanning

00:30:56.550 --> 00:30:57.710
for life-forms
since this started

00:30:57.752 --> 00:30:58.810
and we haven't found anything.

00:30:58.853 --> 00:31:01.048
Maybe we've been looking
in the wrong place.

00:31:01.088 --> 00:31:04.057
I'm betting a species that
spends its time sleeping

00:31:04.091 --> 00:31:05.388
isn't going to be hanging around

00:31:05.426 --> 00:31:07.451
where conventional scans
can locate them.

00:31:07.495 --> 00:31:08.826
So, how do we find them?

00:31:08.863 --> 00:31:10.831
This neurogenic
field you mentioned...

00:31:10.865 --> 00:31:13.732
anyone in a hyper-REM state
would be producing one.

00:31:13.768 --> 00:31:14.792
In theory, yes.

00:31:16.103 --> 00:31:18.196
So if we scan
for other neurogenic fields,

00:31:18.239 --> 00:31:19.831
it might lead us
to the sleeping aliens.

00:31:19.874 --> 00:31:22.206
If you need me,
I'll be on the Bridge.

00:31:33.554 --> 00:31:35.454
Time for a little energy boost,
Commander.

00:31:35.489 --> 00:31:37.150
We don't want you drifting
back to sleep.

00:31:37.191 --> 00:31:38.920
Sorry about the mess,

00:31:38.959 --> 00:31:40.824
but this is what happens
when my repeated requests

00:31:40.861 --> 00:31:43.523
for a larger Sick Bay
fall on deaf ears.

00:31:49.637 --> 00:31:51.662
What is it?

00:31:51.705 --> 00:31:54.105
Scanners have detected
a neurogenic field

00:31:54.141 --> 00:31:56.132
emanating from
beneath the surface of a planet

00:31:56.177 --> 00:31:57.940
less than a light-year
from here.

00:31:57.978 --> 00:32:01.505
Excuse me, Tom, but I've
got to change our course.

00:32:08.754 --> 00:32:10.244
Still dreaming?

00:32:10.289 --> 00:32:11.950
How is that possible?

00:32:12.057 --> 00:32:13.547
I don't know, but that's
what Chakotay said

00:32:13.592 --> 00:32:14.820
right before he vanished.

00:32:14.860 --> 00:32:16.122
That doesn't make any sense.

00:32:16.161 --> 00:32:18.629
He was wide awake
right here with us.

00:32:18.664 --> 00:32:20.689
He said something
about still being asleep

00:32:20.733 --> 00:32:22.792
and then he started tapping
the back of his hand

00:32:22.835 --> 00:32:25.201
like he said he would
to wake up from his lucid dream.

00:32:25.237 --> 00:32:27.432
And then he disappeared.

00:32:29.074 --> 00:32:31.941
The question is:
Where did he go?

00:32:31.977 --> 00:32:34.775
The aliens must
have transported him somewhere.

00:32:34.813 --> 00:32:36.781
Or perhaps he did wake up.

00:32:36.815 --> 00:32:37.873
Tuvok?

00:32:37.916 --> 00:32:41.283
It's possible he was dreaming
all of this.

00:32:41.320 --> 00:32:43.720
Wait a minute.

00:32:43.756 --> 00:32:46.748
If Chakotay was dreaming
and he woke up,

00:32:46.792 --> 00:32:48.384
what are we doing here?

00:32:48.427 --> 00:32:50.759
Perhaps we are dreaming
as well.

00:32:50.796 --> 00:32:52.627
Now I'm lost.

00:32:52.665 --> 00:32:54.292
You're not the only one.

00:32:54.333 --> 00:32:56.893
Consider that we all
experienced nightmares

00:32:56.935 --> 00:32:58.493
about an alien whose people

00:32:58.537 --> 00:33:01.062
apparently live out their lives
in a dream state.

00:33:01.106 --> 00:33:04.269
Perhaps we are in that state
this very moment.

00:33:04.309 --> 00:33:05.241
That's ridiculous.

00:33:05.277 --> 00:33:06.266
We're not asleep.

00:33:06.311 --> 00:33:07.278
Wait.

00:33:07.312 --> 00:33:08.279
When you dream,

00:33:08.313 --> 00:33:10.213
you're rarely aware
that you're sleeping.

00:33:10.249 --> 00:33:12.342
I can understand
how we could mistake dreaming

00:33:12.384 --> 00:33:14.944
for reality,
but that doesn't explain

00:33:14.987 --> 00:33:17.114
how we're all interacting
with one another.

00:33:17.156 --> 00:33:18.714
Maybe we're not.

00:33:18.757 --> 00:33:19.917
Not what?

00:33:19.958 --> 00:33:21.619
Interacting with one another.

00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:24.857
Maybe this is all
one person's dream...

00:33:24.897 --> 00:33:26.364
if, for example, mine...

00:33:26.398 --> 00:33:27.490
and none of you are really here.

00:33:27.533 --> 00:33:29.967
Trust me, Neelix,
I wish I weren't, but I'm here.

00:33:30.035 --> 00:33:31.764
Collective unconsciousness.

00:33:31.804 --> 00:33:34.534
Seven, come here.

00:33:36.375 --> 00:33:39.640
The Borg share
a collective consciousness.

00:33:39.678 --> 00:33:41.373
These aliens
may have somehow induced

00:33:41.413 --> 00:33:43.210
a state
of collective unconsciousness.

00:33:43.248 --> 00:33:47.514
You mean... we're all
sharing the same dream?

00:33:47.553 --> 00:33:49.248
It is possible.

00:33:49.288 --> 00:33:52.155
This is all
fascinating speculation,

00:33:52.191 --> 00:33:53.988
but unless we have proof
to the contrary,

00:33:54.059 --> 00:33:55.993
we have to treat this
like an invasion.

00:33:56.028 --> 00:33:58.292
I managed to open
a Jefferies tube hatch.

00:33:58.330 --> 00:33:59.627
Good work.

00:33:59.665 --> 00:34:01.064
Neelix, Seven, Kim,

00:34:01.100 --> 00:34:03.091
do what you can
to distract the guards.

00:34:03.135 --> 00:34:04.693
We're going to find a way
to retake the ship.

00:34:12.611 --> 00:34:14.943
Looks like a complete
power drain.

00:34:14.980 --> 00:34:17.676
Their dampening field
has shut down the warp core.

00:34:17.716 --> 00:34:18.683
Which begs the question

00:34:18.717 --> 00:34:20.446
of what they intend to do
with an unpowered ship.

00:34:20.486 --> 00:34:23.717
Tuvok, grab some phaser rifles
from the weapons locker.

00:34:25.257 --> 00:34:26.554
Something tells me
that when we try

00:34:26.592 --> 00:34:27.786
to disable the dampening field,

00:34:27.826 --> 00:34:29.350
we're going to get
the aliens' attention.

00:34:29.394 --> 00:34:32.955
It looks like they're using
harmonic inversion technology.

00:34:33.065 --> 00:34:35.727
If I can isolate
the containment frequency,

00:34:35.768 --> 00:34:38.134
I may be able to get
main power back on line.

00:34:43.709 --> 00:34:44.971
That was easy.

00:34:45.077 --> 00:34:47.409
Warning. Warp core breach
in 60 seconds.

00:34:47.446 --> 00:34:48.845
Maybe a little too easy.

00:34:48.881 --> 00:34:49.939
I don't understand.

00:34:49.982 --> 00:34:50.949
Can you eject the core?

00:34:50.983 --> 00:34:52.507
I'm trying.

00:34:52.551 --> 00:34:54.109
It's not working.

00:34:54.153 --> 00:34:56.485
Warp core breach in 50 seconds.

00:34:58.557 --> 00:34:59.990
We've got to get out of here.

00:35:00.058 --> 00:35:02.720
I'm trying to put a containment
field around Engineering.

00:35:02.761 --> 00:35:05.025
Warp core breach in 40 seconds.

00:35:05.063 --> 00:35:07.054
Got it! Let's move!

00:35:08.100 --> 00:35:11.297
I don't understand why you
couldn't eject the core!

00:35:11.336 --> 00:35:13.361
Warp core breach in 30 seconds.

00:35:13.405 --> 00:35:15.873
Something's not right.

00:35:15.908 --> 00:35:17.239
Captain, we must hurry!

00:35:17.276 --> 00:35:18.800
I'm going back in there.

00:35:18.844 --> 00:35:19.868
You'll be killed!

00:35:19.912 --> 00:35:20.901
Warp core breach...

00:35:20.946 --> 00:35:22.538
I think I'm onto something.
You two go!

00:35:22.581 --> 00:35:23.240
Captain!

00:35:23.282 --> 00:35:24.681
That's an order!

00:35:26.018 --> 00:35:27.952
Warp core breach in ten seconds.

00:35:28.020 --> 00:35:31.547
Nine, eight, seven, six...

00:35:32.591 --> 00:35:37.187
five, four, three, two, one.

00:35:47.706 --> 00:35:52.143
Either I've become impervious
to antimatter explosions...

00:35:52.177 --> 00:35:54.441
or we're still dreaming.

00:36:00.285 --> 00:36:02.412
A warp core explosion
should have destroyed the ship.

00:36:02.454 --> 00:36:05.389
If I were awake,
or if any of this were real,

00:36:05.424 --> 00:36:06.914
which it obviously isn't.

00:36:06.992 --> 00:36:08.550
Things just weren't adding up...

00:36:08.594 --> 00:36:12.428
Chakotay's disappearance,
the warp core failing to eject.

00:36:12.464 --> 00:36:14.091
And as Chakotay said

00:36:14.132 --> 00:36:17.397
"lucid dreaming
is about taking control"

00:36:17.436 --> 00:36:19.301
so I... took a chance.

00:36:19.338 --> 00:36:21.329
Surely, there must have been
a less extreme method

00:36:21.373 --> 00:36:22.533
of testing your assumptions.

00:36:22.574 --> 00:36:25.839
As Captain, you shouldn't be
taking chances with your life.

00:36:25.878 --> 00:36:27.937
I'm touched by your concern,
Tuvok.

00:36:28.013 --> 00:36:30.846
Now that we know
this is a dream...

00:36:30.883 --> 00:36:32.714
what do we do?

00:36:32.751 --> 00:36:35.549
I suggest we find a way
to regain consciousness.

00:36:41.727 --> 00:36:43.752
Captain, how did
you wake yourself?

00:36:43.795 --> 00:36:44.887
The same way you did.

00:36:44.930 --> 00:36:45.954
The others?

00:36:45.998 --> 00:36:47.522
They should all be
starting to wake up.

00:36:47.566 --> 00:36:49.898
Rise and shine, Mr. Paris.

00:36:49.935 --> 00:36:52.768
We need to get as far away
from their planet as possible.

00:36:52.804 --> 00:36:53.930
Agreed.

00:36:53.972 --> 00:36:55.963
I'll make the necessary
course correction.

00:36:59.578 --> 00:37:01.045
What is it?

00:37:02.915 --> 00:37:04.906
This isn't real.

00:37:05.017 --> 00:37:06.780
Of course it is.

00:37:08.186 --> 00:37:09.551
See?

00:37:09.588 --> 00:37:11.180
No.

00:37:16.995 --> 00:37:17.927
Doctor?

00:37:17.996 --> 00:37:19.930
He's paranoid... disoriented.

00:37:19.998 --> 00:37:21.226
I suspect much of the crew

00:37:21.266 --> 00:37:23.598
will suffer similar
symptoms when they awake.

00:37:24.603 --> 00:37:26.571
Try to relax, Commander.

00:37:26.605 --> 00:37:27.572
I'm going to sedate you.

00:37:27.606 --> 00:37:29.506
No! I need to wake up,
not sleep!

00:37:29.541 --> 00:37:30.940
I'm here to help you.

00:37:31.009 --> 00:37:33.068
No!

00:37:34.713 --> 00:37:36.408
It's all right, Commander.

00:37:36.448 --> 00:37:38.040
You're awake again.

00:37:41.787 --> 00:37:43.687
What happened?

00:37:43.722 --> 00:37:45.121
You dozed off.

00:37:45.157 --> 00:37:47.591
I couldn't wake myself
like I did before.

00:37:47.626 --> 00:37:49.218
Our proximity
to the neurogenic field

00:37:49.261 --> 00:37:51.286
is making it more difficult
to stay conscious.

00:37:51.330 --> 00:37:53.298
I need to get down there and
find a way to neutralize it.

00:37:53.332 --> 00:37:54.424
Not so fast.

00:37:54.466 --> 00:37:56.900
This is a highly potent
animazine derivative.

00:37:56.935 --> 00:37:58.562
If you feel yourself
falling asleep again,

00:37:58.603 --> 00:37:59.900
you must use it.

00:37:59.938 --> 00:38:03.305
And, Commander, I suggest
we keep an open com line.

00:38:03.342 --> 00:38:05.139
I may need to provide you
with a verbal splash

00:38:05.177 --> 00:38:06.906
of cold water
every now and then.

00:38:13.685 --> 00:38:15.619
It's not working.

00:38:15.654 --> 00:38:17.645
It's safe to assume
that Chakotay and the Doctor

00:38:17.689 --> 00:38:20.123
are making every effort
to wake us from our sleep.

00:38:20.158 --> 00:38:22.149
We have to let the rest of
the crew know what's happening...

00:38:22.194 --> 00:38:23.718
that as long as they know
they're in a dream,

00:38:23.762 --> 00:38:24.922
they can't be harmed.

00:38:24.963 --> 00:38:26.624
And if the aliens
try to stop us?

00:38:26.665 --> 00:38:28.929
Then we turn this dreamworld
of theirs...

00:38:28.967 --> 00:38:30.992
into a nightmare.

00:38:45.150 --> 00:38:47.050
Okay, Doctor...

00:38:47.085 --> 00:38:48.313
I'm in.

00:38:48.353 --> 00:38:49.980
Acknowledged, Commander.

00:39:25.957 --> 00:39:27.083
Stand aside.

00:39:27.125 --> 00:39:29.719
Your weapons are useless
against us.

00:39:29.761 --> 00:39:31.194
You're not fooling anyone.

00:39:31.229 --> 00:39:32.890
We know this is a dream.

00:39:32.931 --> 00:39:34.694
You're confused.

00:39:34.733 --> 00:39:38.225
Actually, I'm finally
seeing things clearly.

00:39:38.270 --> 00:39:40.329
Shoot them.

00:39:43.508 --> 00:39:45.772
Now, stand aside.

00:39:50.882 --> 00:39:53.851
All of you, listen closely.

00:39:53.885 --> 00:39:56.945
What we have to do
is stay in control of the dream.

00:39:56.988 --> 00:39:58.956
If we can do that,

00:39:59.057 --> 00:40:01.287
the aliens shouldn't
be able to hurt us.

00:40:04.262 --> 00:40:07.095
You sound very sure
of yourself, Captain.

00:40:07.132 --> 00:40:09.862
Why shouldn't I be?

00:40:09.901 --> 00:40:11.664
Have you thought
about what's happening

00:40:11.703 --> 00:40:13.295
to your bodies
in the waking world?

00:40:13.338 --> 00:40:15.740
How long do you think
they'll survive

00:40:15.873 --> 00:40:17.238
without nourishment?

00:40:17.274 --> 00:40:18.605
Without physical activity?

00:40:18.642 --> 00:40:22.738
Your bodies are withering
away as we speak.

00:40:22.780 --> 00:40:24.611
You can't stop it.

00:40:24.648 --> 00:40:26.946
Don't be so sure.

00:40:27.084 --> 00:40:28.642
It's some kind of transmitter.

00:40:28.686 --> 00:40:30.984
It looks like they use it
to amplify

00:40:31.088 --> 00:40:32.385
the neurogenic field.

00:40:32.423 --> 00:40:33.981
Can you turn it off?

00:40:34.091 --> 00:40:35.854
I tried knocking it out
with my phaser,

00:40:35.893 --> 00:40:37.827
but there's some kind
of force field.

00:40:41.465 --> 00:40:42.830
Commander?

00:40:42.867 --> 00:40:44.494
I'm sorry.

00:40:44.535 --> 00:40:46.002
I'm having trouble
concentrating.

00:40:46.103 --> 00:40:47.900
Time for your medicine.

00:40:58.849 --> 00:41:01.818
Doctor, this animazine...
it's pretty powerful.

00:41:01.852 --> 00:41:04.753
Yes. And I suggest
you take it immediately.

00:41:04.789 --> 00:41:07.087
These aliens...

00:41:07.124 --> 00:41:09.752
they look pretty frail.

00:41:09.794 --> 00:41:10.954
That's fascinating, Commander.

00:41:10.995 --> 00:41:12.986
Now please inject yourself.

00:41:15.666 --> 00:41:17.725
They probably wouldn't have
the same tolerance

00:41:17.768 --> 00:41:18.962
for stimulants that we do.

00:41:19.003 --> 00:41:20.561
What are you getting at?

00:41:20.604 --> 00:41:22.333
The animazine might be capable

00:41:22.373 --> 00:41:23.772
of waking up
one of these aliens.

00:41:23.808 --> 00:41:25.503
Commander, I'd be
happy to discuss

00:41:25.543 --> 00:41:26.976
comparative pharmacology
with you

00:41:27.077 --> 00:41:29.545
after you administer
your injection.

00:41:29.580 --> 00:41:32.208
Actually... I think
I'm going to give it

00:41:32.249 --> 00:41:33.978
to one
of my sleepy friends here.

00:41:34.051 --> 00:41:36.076
What would that accomplish?

00:41:36.120 --> 00:41:37.519
If I can wake him up,

00:41:37.555 --> 00:41:40.991
I might be able to get him
to deactivate this generator.

00:41:41.091 --> 00:41:42.922
There's not enough animazine
for two doses.

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:45.155
If you fall asleep again,
there's no way I can revive you.

00:41:46.831 --> 00:41:48.992
Doctor, I want you
to go to the Bridge.

00:41:49.033 --> 00:41:50.625
Commander...

00:41:50.668 --> 00:41:52.158
I'm giving you an order!

00:41:52.203 --> 00:41:54.194
Go to the Bridge
and target my com signal

00:41:54.238 --> 00:41:55.330
with a photon torpedo.

00:41:55.372 --> 00:41:56.396
You're delirious.

00:41:56.440 --> 00:41:58.203
You're asking me
to incinerate you.

00:41:58.242 --> 00:41:59.766
Not just me...

00:41:59.810 --> 00:42:02.608
these aliens...

00:42:02.646 --> 00:42:04.876
and their transmitter, too.

00:42:04.915 --> 00:42:06.143
But only if you
don't hear from me

00:42:06.183 --> 00:42:07.650
in five minutes.
Understood?

00:42:07.685 --> 00:42:08.652
Commander...

00:42:08.686 --> 00:42:10.381
Understood?!

00:42:12.356 --> 00:42:13.550
Aye, sir.

00:42:25.436 --> 00:42:26.733
Tell me how to deactivate

00:42:26.770 --> 00:42:29.568
this transmitter,
or I start shooting.

00:42:29.607 --> 00:42:30.938
What happened?

00:42:30.975 --> 00:42:33.671
Looks like he woke up.

00:42:35.479 --> 00:42:37.344
I'll give you five seconds.

00:42:37.381 --> 00:42:40.179
Four...

00:42:40.217 --> 00:42:41.445
three...

00:42:41.485 --> 00:42:43.009
two...

00:42:45.556 --> 00:42:47.786
Chakotay.

00:42:51.195 --> 00:42:53.663
Who's going to help
you now, Captain?

00:42:53.697 --> 00:42:56.530
I found the cavern
and your people.

00:42:56.567 --> 00:42:58.762
I'm there right now
in the waking world.

00:42:58.802 --> 00:43:00.394
And it's all going
to be destroyed

00:43:00.437 --> 00:43:01.597
in less than two minutes

00:43:01.639 --> 00:43:03.800
unless you deactivate
that transmitter.

00:43:03.841 --> 00:43:07.868
If you are there,
you'll be killed, too.

00:43:07.912 --> 00:43:09.880
I think you're lying.

00:43:09.914 --> 00:43:12.439
Oh, believe me,
if I don't contact my ship,

00:43:12.483 --> 00:43:15.418
you and I are both
going to die in our sleep.

00:43:21.592 --> 00:43:26.052
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
Stardate 51471.3.

00:43:26.096 --> 00:43:28.064
With the neurogenic field
neutralized,

00:43:28.098 --> 00:43:31.158
I've been successful
in reviving the entire crew.

00:43:31.201 --> 00:43:33.567
Unfortunately,
the experience has produced

00:43:33.604 --> 00:43:36.072
a troubling side effect
for many of them...

00:43:36.106 --> 00:43:38.165
acute insomnia.

00:43:58.896 --> 00:44:00.124
Computer, lights on.

00:44:03.300 --> 00:44:04.892
Sorry, Commander.

00:44:04.935 --> 00:44:06.562
I didn't mean to frighten you.

00:44:06.603 --> 00:44:08.298
You're not starting breakfast
this early, are you?

00:44:08.339 --> 00:44:10.864
Just rearranging
the supply cabinets.

00:44:10.908 --> 00:44:12.773
I couldn't sleep.

00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:14.038
Neither could I.

00:44:14.078 --> 00:44:16.638
How about a soothing cup of tea?

00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:17.840
Sounds good.

00:44:19.116 --> 00:44:20.208
I know it's silly,

00:44:20.250 --> 00:44:23.083
but every time
I'm about to doze off,

00:44:23.120 --> 00:44:24.314
I... become terrified

00:44:24.355 --> 00:44:26.346
that I won't be able
to wake again.

00:44:28.125 --> 00:44:29.854
You, too?

00:44:29.893 --> 00:44:33.090
We just finished a little late-
night hoverball on the holodeck.

00:44:33.130 --> 00:44:34.597
Three games in a row.

00:44:34.631 --> 00:44:36.189
We were hoping
it would wear us out.

00:44:36.233 --> 00:44:40.135
You know, I could learn to enjoy
these late-night get-togethers.

00:44:40.170 --> 00:44:42.365
Speak for yourself.

00:44:42.406 --> 00:44:44.567
I would kill
for a good night's sleep.

00:44:49.213 --> 00:44:51.545
Neelix, I think it's
time for breakfast.
